# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# RDR-5, RDR-6 and RDR-8: page a long entry with F1, step back with
# Backspace, and leave. The give-back is the point — after the last page
# the panel is gone and the only difference left from the seam-off run is
# the six cells of `Notes` on the bar.
about paging a long entry, and giving the screen back exactly
kind pair
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel
# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), and both
# sides of this pair drive past the challenge, so both need it. Pinned
# by digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 300000000
every 25
# A screen may appear in the two runs a dump apart, because claiming a
# keystroke changes when the program does its own next repaint by less
# than the gap between two stills. One dump of slack, measured (#234).
slack 1

key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201
key F1@10600
key 3@10700
key Return@10800
# Forward, forward, back a page, then out through the far end.
key F1@11200
key F1@11600
key Backspace@12000
key Escape@12400

rect panel 136,8,311,119
rect notes 273,192,311,199

allow 0-9000 none
allow 9025-10599 notes
allow 10600-12400 panel notes
# After Escape the panel is gone and the bar is all that is left.
allow 12600-end notes
